<p><a href="/wiki/Ligand_cone_angle" title="Ligand cone angle">Ligand cone angles</a> are measures of the size of <a href="/wiki/Ligand" title="Ligand">ligands</a> in <a href="/wiki/Coordination_chemistry" class="mw-redirect" title="Coordination chemistry">coordination chemistry</a>.  It is defined as the <a href="/wiki/Solid_angle" title="Solid angle">solid angle</a> formed with the metal at the vertex and the hydrogen atoms at the perimeter of the cone (see figure).<sup id="cite_ref-tolman1970_9-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-tolman1970-9"><span class="cite-bracket">&#91;</span>9<span class="cite-bracket">&#93;</span></a></sup>
</p>
